// Declarative package-build facade.
//
// `nia build` constructs one `Build` for the package containing `build.nia`.
// `packageRoot()` names that package, `buildDir()` is its `.nia-build/` output
// root, and `cacheDir()` is its reusable `.nia-cache/` root. Build scripts
// declare packages, modules, artifacts, actions, and dependencies; the generated
// runner validates and encodes the graph but never executes an action.
//
// Public options are borrowed call descriptors. `Build` copies every retained
// string, path, argument, import, target, and handle relation into
// allocator-owned storage. Handles belong to one live `Build` and are rejected
// when passed to another. `BuildPathView` is always relative to `.nia-build/`;
// package paths use `fs::PathView` together with an explicit package handle.
//
// Artifact options target the invocation artifact by default; `forHost()` is
// the explicit host-tool role. External commands inherit the environment and
// remain uncacheable unless they clear it, declare outputs, and opt into the
// declared-input cache contract. `deinit()` releases the complete retained
// graph and reports the first cleanup error after attempting every release.
// When an owned graph element cannot be released, its containing list remains
// attached so a later `deinit()` call can reach the residual owner.
// `Build::init` returns a `BuildInitAttempt`; callers must retry `finish()` when
// allocator cleanup fails. The attempt publishes the initialized `Build` or
// the original initialization error only after every partial owner is retired.
// Package insertion reserves its owning list before retaining fields. A
// partially initialized package stays in a Build-owned pending slot when
// rollback cleanup fails and is retried by the next insertion or `deinit()`.
// Object and static-archive targets use the same pending-record transaction for
// their retained names and output names.
// Executable targets additionally keep their static-archive handle-list backing
// in the pending record until every owned field is ready for transfer.
// Module insertion appends empty import records only after reserving both list
// levels, so nested import name/path cleanup remains reachable from Build.
// Generated-file and uncacheable steps use a kind-correct pending Step whose
// name and payload owners transfer only after post-reserve initialization.
// Run/test steps keep argument strings in that pending owner. Dependency-edge
// failure preserves the primary error while moving the popped step back to the
// pending slot for cleanup retry.
// Executable and static-archive install steps apply the same transaction to
// their destination strings and producer dependency edge.
// External-command steps attach argument and environment slots before retaining
// their nested strings, and roll back all producer edges as one transaction.
// addTestSuite creates one host executable, its compile step, and its test
// step; the root module can import the complete suite through normal modules.
// Simple aggregate/check/emit steps also use the pending slot, and all
// multi-edge additions use explicit suffix rollback. Build contains no fallible
// cleanup defer paths.
// `fs::File::close` consumes its descriptor before attempting the OS close; a
// caller must not retry it after an error unless it owns a fresh descriptor.

pub(pkg) module commands;
pub(pkg) module core;
pub(pkg) module dependencies;
pub(pkg) module diagnostics;
pub(pkg) module error;
pub(pkg) module handles;
pub(pkg) module lifecycle;
pub(pkg) module modules;
pub(pkg) module ownership;
pub(pkg) module paths;
pub(pkg) module plan;
pub(pkg) module queries;
pub(pkg) module records_cleanup;
pub(pkg) module steps;
pub(pkg) module targets;
pub(pkg) module types;
pub(pkg) module validation;

using pkg::build::core;
